/*
 * Declares the AddressValue class.
 *
 * AddressValue represents a memory operation that retrieves the address of a
 * value. This corresponds to the unary address-of operator (`&`) and produces
 * an lvalue pointer/reference type depending on the semantic context.
 *
 * The operand must itself be an lvalue, since only memory-backed values have an
 * address. The resulting value is always an lvalue, as the address itself can
 * be stored, passed, or manipulated.
 *
 * <hr>
 * 
 * @Package: ymirc        
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::value::memory::address
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/value/memory/address.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created (YYYY-MM-DD): 2021-11-20
 * @Copyright (C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
